  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2x+y,\\,D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le y,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 6\\}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $a$ given that $b=4.$",
